course: dictionary
lesson: 9593
title: Tiny living things: streptococcus
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Streptococcus is a noun, a type of bacteria. Bacteria are tiny living things, far too small to see without a microscope. «Most sore throats are caused by viruses and get better within about a week; some are caused by streptococcus bacteria.» The word after «some are caused by» names what causes those sore throats, so streptococcus must be a kind of germ that causes illness.
explain: Streptococcus bacteria are round and grow in chains, a bit like beads on a string. «Scarlet fever is caused by streptococcus bacteria, gives a rough sandpaper rash, and is easily treated with antibiotics.» The rash is a clue that tells you the illness is different from a simple sore throat.
explain: Use the swap test. Put your meaning into the sentence instead of the word: «Some sore throats are caused by round bacteria that grow in chains.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Streptococcus is a noun, and its plural is streptococci.
fact: Streptococcus means a type of round bacteria that grow in chains.
fact: Some streptococcus bacteria live harmlessly in us, but others cause illnesses such as strep throat and scarlet fever.
fact: Doctors can test for «strep» with a throat swab, and infections are usually treated with antibiotics.
fact: Washing hands and covering coughs helps to stop illnesses spreading.
exercise: «Scarlet fever is caused by streptococcus bacteria.» What does streptococcus mean? | A doctor who tests throats | A tablet you swallow to feel better | A rash that feels like sandpaper | *A type of round bacteria that grow in chains
exercise: Under a microscope, streptococci look like what? | Flat sheets of paper | Tiny stars | *Strings of beads | Long wooden sticks
exercise: What is the plural of streptococcus? | streptococcae | streptococcis | *streptococci | streptococcuses
test: Doctors can find «strep» by using what? | A pair of glasses | *A throat swab | A bandage | A loud whistle
test: Which action helps to stop illnesses spreading? | Sharing drink bottles with friends | Going to bed with the lights on | *Washing hands and covering coughs | Shaking hands with everyone you meet
exam: Which statement matches «Most sore throats are caused by viruses and get better within about a week»? | Every sore throat needs antibiotics straight away | Sore throats never get better | Streptococcus causes every sore throat | *Most sore throats are caused by viruses, and many get better within about a week
